1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
This is the Corsair Queen,

2
00:00:02,624 --> 00:00:06,102
and she isn't in the game you installed.

3
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:11,350
I wrote her this morning, in one small text file,

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,713
and I didn't write any code to do it.

5
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:20,122
By the end of this lecture,

6
00:00:20,572 --> 00:00:24,920
you'll have a boss of your own in that list.

7
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:29,598
You played Siege in the very first lecture.

8
00:00:30,498 --> 00:00:32,672
Raiders come at your starbases,

9
00:00:33,122 --> 00:00:37,035
and you win when the last raider is gone.

10
00:00:37,935 --> 00:00:40,543
Now, if you choose a boss,

11
00:00:40,993 --> 00:00:44,907
something worse arrives when the raiders are nearly beaten.

12
00:00:46,707 --> 00:00:49,315
Four bosses come with the game,

13
00:00:49,765 --> 00:00:54,113
and each one is a single file in a folder.

14
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:59,361
So if you add a file, you've added a boss.

15
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:03,604
Here's the Warlord, and it's two records,

16
00:01:04,054 --> 00:01:06,663
in the shape you already know:

17
00:01:07,113 --> 00:01:10,157
a heading, a fence, and a body.

18
00:01:11,057 --> 00:01:14,100
The first record is the boss herself.

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,348
There's one word alone on a line, the word Boss,

20
00:01:19,798 --> 00:01:23,276
which says what kind of record this is.

21
00:01:24,176 --> 00:01:27,220
Trigger and Low say when she arrives:

22
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:31,148
when a quarter of the raiders are left.

23
00:01:32,048 --> 00:01:35,526
Flies and Fleets say what comes with her,

24
00:01:35,976 --> 00:01:38,150
and Named is her flagship:

25
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:42,078
a name, and then which ship it is.

26
00:01:43,878 --> 00:01:46,487
The second record is a quest,

27
00:01:46,937 --> 00:01:50,850
and you wrote plenty of those in Class 1.

28
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:54,793
It belongs to the Siege's own mission,

29
00:01:55,243 --> 00:01:57,852
the crew needs it to win,

30
00:01:58,302 --> 00:02:03,085
and it's done when the Siege says every raider is gone.

31
00:02:04,285 --> 00:02:06,893
Don't edit the Warlord. Copy it.

32
00:02:07,793 --> 00:02:12,141
And don't paste it back into the game's own folder,

33
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:17,374
because that folder is replaced every time the game is updated.

34
00:02:18,274 --> 00:02:20,013
Yours goes here instead:

35
00:02:20,463 --> 00:02:23,941
common data, and then a folder called bosses.

36
00:02:25,741 --> 00:02:27,915
The Siege reads both folders,

37
00:02:28,365 --> 00:02:33,583
so a file in either one is a boss in the list.

38
00:02:34,483 --> 00:02:36,222
For the file's name,

39
00:02:36,672 --> 00:02:40,150
use small letters and underscores, with no spaces.

40
00:02:41,350 --> 00:02:45,263
Before I change anything, I'm going to run lint,

41
00:02:45,713 --> 00:02:48,322
pointed at my own bosses folder.

42
00:02:49,222 --> 00:02:52,265
And it already has something to say.

43
00:02:53,165 --> 00:02:56,209
My copy still has the Warlord's name,

44
00:02:56,659 --> 00:02:59,702
and the list offers bosses by name,

45
00:03:00,152 --> 00:03:04,500
so only one of the two can be in it.

46
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:11,083
It's a true warning, and it's the first thing we'll fix.

47
00:03:12,283 --> 00:03:15,761
The square brackets hold what the crew reads,

48
00:03:16,211 --> 00:03:19,254
and the round brackets hold the key,

49
00:03:19,704 --> 00:03:23,617
which I make the same as my file's name.

50
00:03:24,517 --> 00:03:26,257
Next is her flagship,

51
00:03:26,707 --> 00:03:31,054
and I'm only changing the first word, the ship's name.

52
00:03:32,854 --> 00:03:34,593
There's one trap here.

53
00:03:35,493 --> 00:03:38,972
A flagship's name has to be one word.

54
00:03:39,872 --> 00:03:43,350
If I type Iron Duke, as two words,

55
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,843
the game reads a ship called Iron,

56
00:03:47,293 --> 00:03:49,467
of a kind called Duke,

57
00:03:49,917 --> 00:03:52,961
and there's no such kind of ship.

58
00:03:53,861 --> 00:03:56,035
Lint does catch that one,

59
00:03:56,485 --> 00:04:00,398
and it shows you the line to write instead.

60
00:04:01,598 --> 00:04:04,641
Now for the part you're here for.

61
00:04:05,541 --> 00:04:09,454
Under the first fence goes one line about her.

62
00:04:10,354 --> 00:04:16,441
That one's a note for you, and for anyone you give the file to,

63
00:04:16,891 --> 00:04:20,804
because the game doesn't show it to the crew.

64
00:04:21,704 --> 00:04:23,443
The objective is different,

65
00:04:23,893 --> 00:04:26,502
since the crew does read that.

66
00:04:27,402 --> 00:04:31,315
So it gets a new name, a new key,

67
00:04:31,765 --> 00:04:36,113
what it pays, and a sentence in your own voice.

68
00:04:37,913 --> 00:04:41,826
Leave the five lines in the middle alone today,

69
00:04:42,276 --> 00:04:45,754
and keep the word credits after the number,

70
00:04:46,204 --> 00:04:47,943
or nothing gets paid.

71
00:04:48,843 --> 00:04:51,017
Then save, run lint again,

72
00:04:51,467 --> 00:04:54,076
and this time it says clean.

73
00:04:55,276 --> 00:05:01,363
To see her, I start the game the way you have since Class 1,

74
00:05:01,813 --> 00:05:04,857
but with Legendary Missions as the mission,

75
00:05:05,307 --> 00:05:09,654
and with no map on the end of the line.

76
00:05:10,554 --> 00:05:14,033
That leaves the server on the start screen.

77
00:05:14,933 --> 00:05:17,107
Siege is on the left,

78
00:05:17,557 --> 00:05:23,209
and on the right is the Options panel, with a line called Boss.

79
00:05:25,009 --> 00:05:28,922
And there she is, under the game's own four.

80
00:05:29,822 --> 00:05:31,996
If she's missing for you,

81
00:05:32,446 --> 00:05:35,054
the file's in the wrong folder,

82
00:05:35,504 --> 00:05:39,852
or the game was already running when you saved it.

83
00:05:41,052 --> 00:05:46,704
At twenty-five percent, you'd fight for a long time before she showed up.

84
00:05:47,604 --> 00:05:51,083
So for testing, I set Low to ninety.

85
00:05:51,983 --> 00:05:56,330
Now she comes when one raider in ten is gone,

86
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:59,824
which here is after the second kill.

87
00:06:01,624 --> 00:06:04,667
There's the Morrigan, with her two fleets,

88
00:06:05,117 --> 00:06:09,900
and there's my objective in the Quest Log, in my words.

89
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,974
Notice that nothing announced her.

90
00:06:13,424 --> 00:06:17,772
The game doesn't tell the crew a boss has arrived,

91
00:06:18,222 --> 00:06:22,570
and we'll do something about that later in the class.

92
00:06:23,470 --> 00:06:25,209
When you've finished testing,

93
00:06:25,659 --> 00:06:27,833
put Low back to twenty-five.

94
00:06:29,033 --> 00:06:32,076
This is why she lives out here.

95
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:35,150
You can update the game,

96
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,209
and this folder is left alone.

97
00:06:39,109 --> 00:06:42,587
It's still one file on one computer, though,

98
00:06:43,037 --> 00:06:45,646
so keep a copy somewhere else,

99
00:06:46,096 --> 00:06:49,139
the way you would with a manuscript.

100
00:06:50,939 --> 00:06:56,591
And to give her to a friend, you send them that one file.

101
00:06:57,491 --> 00:07:01,404
Now make a second boss, from your own story.

102
00:07:02,304 --> 00:07:04,913
Next time, we change the numbers.
